<title>GREECE: SIGMA GETS TOP MARKS IN EUROPEAN BROKERS SURVEY - GLOBAL INVESTOR.</title>
<headline>SIGMA GETS TOP MARKS IN EUROPEAN BROKERS SURVEY - GLOBAL INVESTOR.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Athens stock exchange member firm</p>
<p>Sigma Securities got top marks in Global Investor's 1996</p>
<p>pan-European brokers survey for research and execution in</p>
<p>Greece, the international fund management monthly said in its</p>
<p>October issue.</p>
<p>In its country-by-country analysis featuring &quot;the best and</p>
<p>the rest&quot;, Global Investor said this year's poll asked European</p>
<p>fund managers to pick their favourite firms for quality equity</p>
<p>research and execution.</p>
<p>The poll's results for Greece have as follows:</p>
<p>Research rankings</p>
<p>    1996	1995	  Firm			  %</p>
<p>     1	   2	    Sigma Securities	 44</p>
<p>     2	   1	    Schroder Securities    20</p>
<p>     3	   --	   SBC Warburg		15</p>
<p>     4	   4	    Alpha Brokerage	   7</p>
<p>     5	   --	   Salomon Brothers	  5</p>
<p>Global Investor said local broker Sigma Securities took the</p>
<p>top position by a comfortable margin from last year's winner</p>
<p>Schroder Securities.</p>
<p>&quot;Sigma is conspicuous in the professionalism of its</p>
<p>approach. That separates it from their Greek competitors. The</p>
<p>depth of coverage separates Sigma from their foreign</p>
<p>competition,&quot; a fund manager comments.</p>
<p>Execution rankings</p>
<p>    1996	1995	   Firm			  %</p>
<p>     1	   1	     Sigma Securities	  51</p>
<p>     2	   2	     Alpha Brokerage	   13</p>
<p>     3	   --	    SBC Warburg		 12</p>
<p>     4	   --	    Schroder Securities     10</p>
<p>     5	   --	    Salomon Brothers	   6</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
